Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  

• SAMPLE_CONTENTS."binary": filter out binary files (non‑binary ⇒ FALSE)  
• SAMPLE_CONTENTS."sample_path": locate Swift files (path ends with “.swift”)  
• SAMPLE_CONTENTS."copies": how many times that exact file (uniquely defined by its "id") occurs in different repos – we want the highest value  
• SAMPLE_CONTENTS."id": unique SHA for each file; guarantees we treat every file only once  
• SAMPLE_CONTENTS."sample_repo_name": tells which repository a particular file copy is taken from – needed for the final repo name  
• Optional ─ LANGUAGES."language": could be joined if we wished to restrict to Swift‑tagged repos (not required here)

Typical conditions that will be useful  

1. "binary" = FALSE  
2. "sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift' (case‑insensitive match)  
3. ORDER BY "copies" DESC to find the “most copied” file  
4. LIMIT 1 after ordering to return only the top result  
5. GROUP BY or DISTINCT when exploring or counting values

Below are ten Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that progress from simple exploration to the final answer.  
All identifiers are enclosed in double quotes and the database / schema / table names are adjusted to the ones provided.

```sql
--Description: 1) Look at any rows inside SAMPLE_CONTENTS just to understand the shape of data.
SELECT * 
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Show 20 non‑binary rows (any language) to verify “binary” flag.
SELECT "id", "sample_repo_name", "sample_path", "binary" 
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"
WHERE "binary" = FALSE
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Display 20 Swift files (regardless of binary) to confirm the extension filter.
SELECT "id", "sample_repo_name", "sample_path", "binary"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"
WHERE "sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Combine both filters: non‑binary Swift files only.
SELECT "id", "sample_repo_name", "sample_path", "copies"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"
WHERE "binary" = FALSE
  AND "sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Find the 20 most copied non‑binary Swift files (highest “copies” first).
SELECT "id", "sample_repo_name", "sample_path", "copies"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"
WHERE "binary" = FALSE
  AND "sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift'
ORDER BY "copies" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Check how many distinct repos contain non‑binary Swift files (quick count sample).
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT "sample_repo_name") AS "swift_repo_count"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"
WHERE "binary" = FALSE
  AND "sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift';
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Show top 20 repositories ranked by the maximum “copies” value of any Swift file they host.
SELECT "sample_repo_name",
       MAX("copies") AS "max_copies_for_a_swift_file"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"
WHERE "binary" = FALSE
  AND "sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift'
GROUP BY "sample_repo_name"
ORDER BY "max_copies_for_a_swift_file" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Retrieve the single most copied non‑binary Swift file (its id, path, copies, repo).
SELECT "id", "sample_repo_name", "sample_path", "copies"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"
WHERE "binary" = FALSE
  AND "sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift'
ORDER BY "copies" DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Same as #8 but also bring “size” and a sample of the content to understand the file.
SELECT "id", "sample_repo_name", "sample_path", "copies", "size",
       SUBSTR("content", 1, 200) AS "first_200_chars"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"
WHERE "binary" = FALSE
  AND "sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift'
ORDER BY "copies" DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Final query – returns only the repository name that contains the most copied non‑binary Swift file.
SELECT "sample_repo_name"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"
WHERE "binary" = FALSE
  AND "sample_path" ILIKE '%.swift'
ORDER BY "copies" DESC
LIMIT 1;
```
